

I want to build a front end payroll/accounting application suite that handles crypto payments natively. Should accept some fiat ramp third party integration but natively handle Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana and Nervos Network. Brainstorm plan time. Are there any open source payroll applications that would be a good fork candidate to build from?


Yes. Best fork candidates:


1. ERPNext + Frappe HR — strongest candidate
Best fit if you want a real payroll/accounting suite, not just invoices. ERPNext has accounting, HR, expenses, assets, purchasing, sales, and financial reporting; Frappe HR adds payroll, taxation, employee lifecycle, leave, attendance, expense claims, etc. 
Why fork it: mature ERP foundation, Python/Frappe framework, GPL, already models employees, salary slips, journals, tax components.
Crypto angle: add crypto wallets/accounts as first-class payment rails, then post every crypto payout as accounting journal entries.


2. Bigcapital — best modern accounting core
Bigcapital is open-source accounting/inventory software focused on bookkeeping automation, financial statements, reports, and business finance workflows. 
Why fork it: cleaner modern product surface than ERPNext.
Weakness: not a full payroll/HR stack yet, so you’d need to build payroll more heavily.


3. Akaunting — good small-business accounting base
Akaunting is Laravel/Vue/Tailwind, has invoices, bills, expenses, REST API, modular app-store style architecture. 
Why fork it: likely easier frontend/product iteration.
Weakness: payroll depth may be limited; better for “crypto accounting + contractor payments” than serious payroll.


4. Dolibarr — pragmatic SMB ERP
Dolibarr is a modular open-source ERP/CRM for contacts, suppliers, invoices, orders, stocks, agenda, and accounting. 
Why fork it: stable, modular, SMB friendly.
Weakness: PHP legacy feel; less attractive if you want a slick crypto-native UI.


5. Odoo Community + OCA payroll — powerful but licensing/module complexity
Odoo has payroll docs and the Community/Enterprise split; OCA provides community payroll modules under AGPL-style licensing. 
Why fork it: huge ecosystem.
Weakness: payroll/accounting features can drift into Enterprise or third-party module complexity.


My pick: ERPNext/Frappe HR as the backend/accounting/payroll engine, with a custom crypto-native frontend. Build your suite as a new “Crypto Payroll” Frappe app rather than hard-forking everything initially.


Core modules I’d plan:


Payroll core: employees, contractors, salary rules, payslips, tax withholding, super/benefits, reimbursements.


Crypto treasury: BTC, ETH, SOL, CKB wallets; hot/cold wallet separation; xpub/watch-only mode; address book; approval queues.


Payment engine: batch payroll runs, per-worker preferred asset, fiat-denominated salary converted at execution, transaction status tracking.


Accounting bridge: every payout creates journal entries: salary expense, tax liability, super/benefit liability, crypto asset movement, FX gain/loss.


Compliance layer: payslip fiat value, crypto value, timestamped FX rate, transaction hash, network fee, audit log.


Third-party fiat ramps: Stripe, Coinbase Commerce, Transak, MoonPay, Banxa, or regional partners later. Keep this as an adapter layer, not core logic.


For MVP: contractor/vendor crypto payouts + accounting export first. Full employee payroll compliance is the hard part.



Give me a full featured scaffold I can feed a coding agent on my pc to start building. Run with your recommendations on fork candidate. What’s the most universal front end for Mac/windows/linux compatibility. My stack leans toward react based generally.


For maximum Mac/Windows/Linux compatibility with React, use:

React + Vite + TypeScript as the core web app, then package it with Electron for desktop. Electron bundles Chromium/Node and runs across macOS, Windows, and Linux; Tauri is leaner and excellent, but Electron is still the most universal/predictable target. Tauri supports any frontend and cross-platform builds too, so keep the app shell abstract enough to swap later.  

Backend recommendation: ERPNext/Frappe HR base, extended via a custom Frappe app rather than a hard fork at first. ERPNext is GPL-3.0, open-source, and already covers accounting/HR/payroll foundations.  

